     28
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Pairs of (InternationalFixedDate, expected ISO LocalDate) used to verify that converting an IFC date to a LocalDate yields the correct Gregorian date. The IFC calendar has 13 months of 28 days each, plus a Year Day (month 13 day 29) and, in leap years, a Leap Day (month 6 day 29). These extra days shift the mapping relative to the Gregorian calendar. Groups below cover: - Non-leap year (year 1): basic dates and the Sol/month-7 boundary - Non-leap year (year 1): end-of-year (Year Day) mapping - Leap year (year 4): Sol month with Leap Day, and end-of-year - Century non-leap year (year 100): Sol boundary without Leap Day - 400-year leap year (year 400): Sol boundary with Leap Day - Historical spot checks (1582, 1945, 2012)"
   },
